hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1445","Salam bin Junada told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais Al-Farra’, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah bin Abi Sarh, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “delivered a sermon on the day of Eid on his camel.” Abu Bakr said: This word has two meanings, one of which is that he delivered the sermon standing, not sitting, and the second is that he delivered the sermon on the ground. Such as Abu Sa’id’s denial of Marwan when he took out the pulpit, and he said: He did not take out the pulpit."
